Date:   Tue Sep 22 19:02:41 2026 +0800

    test(frontend): per-surface before/after readings for the wizard hint, and bytes_changed in the kill receipts (ORD-0221)
    
    Body innerText cannot answer "is this on screen": .v8-sr-only is clipped to 1px, not
    removed, so a body-text check counts a screen-reader sentence as visible.  The new spec
    reads each surface's own text plus its own box and computed opacity, and records the
    visible hint and the live region separately.  The harness now prints anchor_bytes and
    bytes_changed, and killU2 adds the direction killU1 never covered (caveat kept, number
    dropped).  killV1 is re-run against the per-surface node as well: it survives both, which
    is the measurement that explains the original survivor.

